1
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:10,120
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:10,920
Keke.

3
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:13,560
The answer to that problem

4
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:15,760
was my message to you.

5
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:23,960
Qin Ming!

6
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,580
(Based on the novel
Doctor Qin: Executer)

7
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:42,160
Keke!

8
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:47,480
Why?

9
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,240
Why?

10
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:59,000
Keke!

11
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:22,020
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 20=

12
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:01,160
The answer to that question is,

13
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,360
no matter where point P is,

14
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,960
as long as the sum
of the distances from you and me

15
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,840
stays constant,

16
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:12,400
the path is a perfect ellipse.

17
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,680
Keke.

18
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,600
Why?

19
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:20,720
Today

20
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,400
is the final judgment.

21
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:24,840
On us.

22
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,240
On you.

23
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:28,760
On myself.

24
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:33,600
Qin Ming.

25
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,040
Officer Qin.

26
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,760
If I run away from here today,

27
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,000
would you pretend you never saw it?

28
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:48,520
Qin Ming.

29
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,040
Don't hesitate.

30
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:53,400
You shouldn't hesitate.

31
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,040
Once a person makes a mistake,

32
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:57,760
they'll make more mistakes

33
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,160
trying to make up for it.

34
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:05,160
Jin Keke has already made
too many mistakes.

35
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,880
Qin Ming can't protect her anymore.

36
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,280
(Police)

37
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:22,360
What's going on?

38
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,120
Qin?

39
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,040
Everyone stay alert.

40
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,160
The suspect is armed.

41
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,840
The hostage is in extreme danger.

42
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,000
Requesting SWAT backup.

43
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,280
(The day I dropped out,)

44
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:32,040
(when you stopped me,)

45
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:35,200
(I really wanted to
tell you everything.)

46
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,360
That way I could

47
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,960
grab onto a lifeline.

48
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,960
But I couldn't bear to

49
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:46,440
drag you down into that kind of abyss.

50
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,680
I'd rather fall

51
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,280
into that kind of bottomless abyss
all by myself.

52
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,000
Stop right there!

53
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:18,880
You're Jin Keke, right?

54
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,470
Hey, hey.

55
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,240
Did your teachers ever teach you
that children

56
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,680
are responsible
for their parents' debts?

57
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,240
How are you gonna pay off

58
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,600
your father's debt?

59
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,960
I heard your grandma's really sick.

60
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,200
You wanna save her?

61
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,680
Today I'm gonna teach you
your first lesson.

62
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:14,280
How to use your own value

63
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:16,400
to get what you want.

64
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:19,800
Get in.

65
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:22,520
Or you can hold

66
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,200
onto your ridiculous pride

67
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:26,200
and let your grandma wait

68
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:28,760
until she stops breathing.

69
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,680
(At first,)

70
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,680
(I screamed for help.)

71
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:13,920
(But that night I learned)

72
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,320
(that despair has a taste.)

73
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:18,960
(It's the metallic taste of blood
on the tongue.)

74
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,880
(It's the disgusting smell of smoke
in his mouth.)

75
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:25,000
(And the salty taste of my own tears.)

76
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:28,760
I thought that night was hell.

77
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:33,520
Turns out it was just
the doorway to hell.

78
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:37,800
What Zhang Xiaodong enjoyed
wasn't violence.

79
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:39,480
He enjoyed the process

80
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:43,800
of turning people
into something less than human.

81
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,520
He and his helpers

82
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,200
trampled everyone's dignity

83
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,120
into dirt.

84
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:05,480
Shi.

85
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:07,120
Come on, Sanhao.

86
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:09,200
Come on, missy.

87
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,480
You gotta finish it.

88
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,160
Saving it for the next life?

89
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,400
Just down it.

90
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,560
It's not even that much.

91
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:40,720
Is it my liquor

92
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:42,960
you don't like,

93
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,320
or the hot pot?

94
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:46,680
Or the place?

95
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:48,880
None of it?

96
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,000
I get it.

97
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:52,720
So you just don't like me.

98
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:58,120
Answer his question!

99
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:03,360
Sir, I... I'm allergic to alcohol.

100
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,200
Allergic?

101
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:07,760
I love me some allergic reactions!

102
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:16,280
Let's see where you're breaking out.

103
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,320
Sir... sir!

104
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:19,560
Where are you breaking out?

105
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:19,960
Ms. Su!

106
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,880
Where are you breaking out?

107
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:21,680
Ms. Su!

108
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:23,120
- Let me see.
- Ms. Su!

109
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:25,120
Ms. Su.

110
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:37,680
So boring.

111
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,400
That's enough.

112
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,080
You're such a waste.

113
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,760
Can't even handle a man.

114
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:07,120
Why did I even bring you out?

115
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,400
And you expect me to help you?

116
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,400
You deserve to be treated like dirt.

117
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:35,480
Go ahead and cry.

118
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,920
(From those days on,)

119
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,600
(no matter where I hid,)

120
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,920
(those demons would always find me.)

121
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:45,920
(What they wanted to toy with)

122
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,480
(wasn't just my body,)

123
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,400
(but also my dignity and soul,)

124
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:53,200
(which meant nothing to them.)

125
00:09:57,600 --> 00:10:00,560
Keke, you think killing those people

126
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,440
will pull the you

127
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:03,880
who was humiliated back then

128
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,080
out of the darkness?

129
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,240
You can't.

130
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,400
You'll only sink deeper.

131
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:13,520
Qin Ming.

132
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:16,200
Don't give me that look!

133
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,680
You think what you're seeing
and hearing now

134
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,200
is all of hell?

135
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,680
You forensic examiners

136
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:25,080
love reconstructing scenes, don't you?

137
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:28,240
You piece together your so-called truth

138
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,360
from bodies and evidence.

139
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,360
But let me tell you,

140
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:34,200
everything you painstakingly reconstruct

141
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,560
doesn't even

142
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:37,840
scratch the surface...

143
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:40,560
of the hell we actually lived through.

144
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,840
The truth you can never reconstruct

145
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:45,120
is my reality,

146
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:49,080
our reality, every single day and night!

147
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,400
Is Qin Ming in danger?

148
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,240
Not right now.

149
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,200
Didn't you say Jin Keke was in danger?

150
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,440
Qin Ming said it himself.

151
00:10:58,280 --> 00:10:59,080
Sniper,

152
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:00,760
if Qin Ming is in danger,

153
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:02,160
take out the suspect immediately.

154
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,600
Can you really imagine

155
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,800
what we've been through?

156
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,280
Keke.

157
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,280
Every clue I found,

158
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,280
every body I dissected,

159
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,240
and every bit of truth
I pieced together...

160
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:30,920
All I could see in my head

161
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:34,480
was what you might have gone through.

162
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,400
But I didn't dare think.

163
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,200
I didn't dare think
about how much more you went through

164
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,520
that I don't know about.

165
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,240
I didn't dare remember either.

166
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,800
I didn't dare remember
that the day you left,

167
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:49,800
I blamed you.

168
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,640
I blamed you for leaving without a word.

169
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:53,800
I blamed you for hiding the truth.

170
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,040
I'm sorry, Keke.

171
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:57,920
I came too late.

172
00:11:58,800 --> 00:11:59,680
I found out

173
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:01,080
about all of this too late.

174
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,000
I...

175
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:07,880
didn't grab your hand sooner.

176
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,520
I'm sorry.

177
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,240
Jin Keke!

178
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:29,840
You're surrounded!

179
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:32,240
Whatever you're going through,
you can tell us.

180
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:33,600
Don't hurt the hostage!

181
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,800
Keke, what are you doing?

182
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,440
Keke, put it down!

183
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,240
For Xia Wen.

184
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:09,800
Keke.

185
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:12,960
Keke.

186
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,200
Let's... let's go to the police.

187
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:22,320
I haven't decided yet.

188
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:31,040
Could you

189
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,200
hold onto this for me?

190
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,600
Why not go to the police?

191
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:50,740
(Meet me at the base tomorrow at 8 PM.
Got something to tell you, by Qin Ming!)

192
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,040
Keke.

193
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,400
So you two...

194
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:05,240
What are you doing?

195
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:11,000
I'm not going.

196
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,240
I need to go home and cook for my dad.

197
00:14:31,610 --> 00:14:32,530
Oh,

198
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,000
don't worry.

199
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,880
The note's already in her hands.

200
00:14:37,760 --> 00:14:38,560
Come on.

201
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,240
My work's on you now.

202
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:44,320
(Meet me at the base tomorrow at 8 PM.
Got something to tell you, by Qin Ming!)

203
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:45,840
You're not going to meet him tonight?

204
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:49,240
I need money.

205
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,120
Sir.

206
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,600
To Fengshan Flower Fields?

207
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,240
Hello, sir.

208
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:27,400
Young lady, what are you here for?

209
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:30,200
Well, I'm here

210
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:32,440
for Zhang Xiaoya's birthday.

211
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,240
Sorry about that.

212
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:36,240
Welcome.

213
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:38,640
Take a left up ahead and you're there.

214
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:41,800
Thank you.

215
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:46,120
Xiaoya, happy birthday!

216
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,280
Let's take a photo together?

217
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:48,960
Come on.

218
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:00,920
(You two come too.)

219
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:01,960
(What are you hiding there for?)

220
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,040
(The star stands in the center.)

221
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:19,440
Keke.

222
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:20,920
Keke.

223
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:30,000
Wen, why... why are you here?

224
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,200
You have to meet him.

225
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:34,760
(Meet me at the base tomorrow at 8 PM.
Got something to tell you, by Qin Ming!)

226
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:36,400
Qin... Qin Ming likes you.

227
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,520
I can tell.

228
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:40,080
I can't go.

229
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:44,200
Qin Ming has a bright future
ahead of him.

230
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:47,080
But I'm already like this...

231
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:48,320
Already like what?

232
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:50,320
You can have a bright future too.

233
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:52,440
You know what?

234
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,200
I've already figured out a way
to help you.

235
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,440
You don't have to worry.

236
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:56,480
Just go.

237
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:00,080
No, Wen.

238
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,400
This... this is too dangerous.

239
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:04,840
You... you can't take that risk.

240
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:07,520
I'm going to get them to wipe
your dad's debt clean.

241
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:09,040
That way you'll be free soon.

242
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:10,480
(Keke?)

243
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:13,320
Keke, hurry.

244
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:15,480
Wait for me to come back.

245
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:16,240
Wait for me.

246
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:25,840
Let me take you to change clothes.

247
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,240
We'll have Mr. Chen drive you back.

248
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:12,320
Who are you?

249
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:14,280
You're Xiaoya, right?

250
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:15,440
Happy birthday.

251
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,840
I'm Jin Keke's classmate.

252
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,200
Jin Keke?

253
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:20,800
Who's Jin Keke?

254
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:23,480
Xiaoxue. I'm Xiaoxue's classmate.

255
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,800
Then what are you doing
in my dad's office?

256
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:30,120
Your father...

257
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:34,200
I came to talk to your dad
about something.

258
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,000
About Xiaoxue.

259
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:42,200
Do you know what my dad did

260
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,240
to Xiaoxue?

261
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:46,520
(Wang,)

262
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:48,080
(I got something good recently.)

263
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:50,640
(Then I'm really honored.)

264
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,200
Hide in there for now.

265
00:19:57,840 --> 00:19:58,640
Xiaoya?

266
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:00,320
Why are you here?

267
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:02,080
Not downstairs greeting your classmates?

268
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:06,280
I'm just gonna run downstairs for a bit.

269
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:10,320
Xia Wen

270
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:14,520
was in Zhang Xiaodong's room?

271
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:18,720
(Keke.)

272
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:21,480
Who actually killed Xia Wen?

273
00:20:31,990 --> 00:20:36,180
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

274
00:20:36,740 --> 00:20:40,820
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

275
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:45,150
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

276
00:20:45,570 --> 00:20:49,510
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

277
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:02,340
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

278
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:05,340
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

279
00:21:05,830 --> 00:21:09,460
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

280
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:13,690
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

281
00:21:13,690 --> 00:21:18,400
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

282
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:22,870
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

283
00:21:23,460 --> 00:21:27,200
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

284
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:31,460
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

285
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:44,470
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

286
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:48,810
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

287
00:21:48,810 --> 00:21:52,590
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

288
00:21:52,590 --> 00:21:55,490
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

289
00:21:55,490 --> 00:22:00,300
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

290
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:04,900
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

291
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:07,240
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

292
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:09,310
♪We stop here in this night♪

293
00:22:09,310 --> 00:22:13,740
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

294
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:19,590
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

295
00:22:22,190 --> 00:22:28,700
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

296
